I am in the metro.
The train is moving fast.
I look above the door.
There is the metro's route map there.
There are many different lines on the map.
I do not understand anything.
I need to go to another line.
An older woman is sitting near me.
I talk to her.
"Excuse me, aunty," I ask.
"I need to go to another line."
"At which station do I need to get off?"
Aunty looks toward the map.
She smiles affectionately.
"You need to get off at the next junction," she says.
"There you need to board another train."
"That train goes straight toward the sea."
"Thank you, aunty," I say happily.
Now I know the correct station.
I sit comfortably on my seat.
